  "id": "coldwatermuseum",
  "note": "COLDWATER MUSEUM — the museum on Kiln Lane, four columns and a pediment on a building one room deep.\n\nThe tile's prose: the portico is stone, correct, and about two and a half times the architectural\nseriousness the shed behind it can support. Cut into the pediment, spaced by somebody who ran out\nof room by the fourth word: THE COLDWATER MVSEVM OF THE WORLD BEFORE. The doors are open in the day,\nthere is no charge, and a slotted box on a post beside them says DONATIONS and is almost empty.\n\nSo the portico is the building: three stone steps, four columns with capitals, an entablature with\nthe inscription on the frieze, and a pediment stepped up in three courses. The shed behind it is\nplainly lower, narrower and brick, and the difference is the joke. The doors are lit when it is\nopen.",
  "pal": "ty_past",
